        "description": "Converts a deep learning model to an Esri classifier definition file (.ecd).",
        "in_classification_info_json.descr": "The class information JSON file. See the JSON file example above.",
        "in_classification_info_json.title": "Input Esri Extra Info File",
        "in_deep_learning_model.descr": "The binary model file generated by a deep learning package such as Google TensorFlow, Microsoft CNTK, or similar application.",
        "in_deep_learning_model.title": "Input Deep Learning Model File",
        "out_classifier_definition.descr": "<xdoc><p>The .ecd file that can be used in the <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Classify</span> function and Classify Raster tool.</p><p>The .ecd output file only works as input to the Esri Python <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Classify</span> or <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Detect</span> adaptor function.</p></xdoc>",
        "out_classifier_definition.title": "Output Classifier Definition File",
        "summary": "<xdoc><p>Converts a deep learning model to an Esri classifier definition file (.ecd).</p><note type=\"legacy\"/><p group=\"note\">This is a deprecated tool. This functionality has been replaced by the Export Training Data For Deep Learning tool that creates classification information for use in the deep learning model.</p><p>This tool adds missing class information to the model. Deep learning binary model files generated by Google TensorFlow, Microsoft CNTK, or similar applications are supported.</p><p>To utilize the deep learning .ecd file, the deep learning framework must be installed on your computer. The .ecd output file will only work as input to the Esri Python <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Classify</span> or <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Detect</span> adaptor function. The class information JSON file allows you to add useful information to the .ecd file not included in the deep learning binary model such as class names, class colors for rendering the classified output, and other standard information. See the JSON file example below for details.</p></xdoc>",
        "title": "Deep Learning Model To Ecd"
    }
}
